%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0ca23d3e41cd5424c9ec72c610ef25a4, type: 3}
  m_Name: EvilEntityconclusion
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  autoFocusSpeaker: 1
  screens:
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 7856103185826971653
    - rid: 7856103185826971654
    - rid: 7856103185826971655
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0afee15b7c0b2ad4481946e7b9820870, type: 2}
    dialog: Hello again.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 7856103185826971656
    - rid: 7856103185826971657
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: Yes, yes, I've returned.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0afee15b7c0b2ad4481946e7b9820870, type: 2}
    dialog: Oh... you're here, too.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: Anyway, how would I go about adding a...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: Whitelist to the interface.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0afee15b7c0b2ad4481946e7b9820870, type: 2}
    dialog: A... whitelist?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: Yes, a list of entities, or objects, that are allowed access to certain...
      priveleges or functions.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0afee15b7c0b2ad4481946e7b9820870, type: 2}
    dialog: Ah, there's already a function for the opposite of that.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: You added a blacklist function to the interface? Why?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: I thought the point was that it could interact with any sentient being...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0afee15b7c0b2ad4481946e7b9820870, type: 2}
    dialog: If you'd believe it, it's because I thought that beings should be free
      to opt-out of the... experience.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: I'm beginning to think I made a mistake working with you.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0afee15b7c0b2ad4481946e7b9820870, type: 2}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 7856103185826971710
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0afee15b7c0b2ad4481946e7b9820870, type: 2}
    dialog: Anyway, what are you planning on doing with your "whitelist?"
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 7856103185826971711
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: You've seen what {mc}'s been up to-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: That boy's newfound apathy toward life is hardly conducive to the narrative
      I'm attempting to weave.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0afee15b7c0b2ad4481946e7b9820870, type: 2}
    dialog: Just wipe his mind, then. Simple solution.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: You know why that wouldn't work-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: The girls already know too, and for some reason {Player} has been cooperating
      with them!
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0afee15b7c0b2ad4481946e7b9820870, type: 2}
    dialog: Is that the name of the higher entity you made the interface for?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: That's what they go by.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: I'm... surprised Natsuki was even able to ask what their name was...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: When porting everything over I made sure that "input name" prompt was
      a one-and-done deal for the title scene-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0afee15b7c0b2ad4481946e7b9820870, type: 2}
    dialog: Like you said, they're from outside of the Dream, too.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0afee15b7c0b2ad4481946e7b9820870, type: 2}
    dialog: They have incredible influence on this world, even if they don't know
      it.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: Yeah, but this world has a completely different ruleset from-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: You know what, nevermind.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: Haaahh...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0afee15b7c0b2ad4481946e7b9820870, type: 2}
    dialog: Since you're here, I've got a question for you.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: Yes, what is it?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0afee15b7c0b2ad4481946e7b9820870, type: 2}
    dialog: I'm curious as to why you're stoking the flames of war in the hearts
      of the Dominion.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: Ah, that's actually pretty simple.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: 'There''s sorta two reasons why:'
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: The first, more long-term, reason is that a potential conflict with the
      Thalmor-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: Who are undoubtedly the current antagonists of the Elder Scrolls-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: Has been gnawing at the minds of Skyrim players pretty much since it
      came out.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: People have made their own material about what might happen in a Second
      Great War-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: There's even a pretty interesting mod that basically extends the Civil
      War mechanics to fit the Dominion v.s. the Forces of Man.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: So I figured it would be an... interesting area to explore while everyone's
      here.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0afee15b7c0b2ad4481946e7b9820870, type: 2}
    dialog: While everyone's here...?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0afee15b7c0b2ad4481946e7b9820870, type: 2}
    dialog: Are you planning on taking your little family elsewhere?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: I haven't finalized that decision yet.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: It'll certainly depend on how well-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: And how quickly- things progress here.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: 'Anyway, the second reason was fairly simple:'
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: '{mc} pretty much had it figured out when he complained that {Player}
      was just being manipulative-'
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: Putting the girls into harms way just seemed like a pretty obvious way
      to get him into action.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: Whether he wants to admit it or not, {mc} has gotten pretty attached.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0afee15b7c0b2ad4481946e7b9820870, type: 2}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0afee15b7c0b2ad4481946e7b9820870, type: 2}
    dialog: Why not just forcefully take the mask from {mc} and place it somewhere
      he can't get it, like here?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: Well, that wouldn't really address the root of the issue.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0afee15b7c0b2ad4481946e7b9820870, type: 2}
    dialog: Neither does "baiting" him back into action through threats to his loved
      ones.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: Maybe, but it ties into what I'm already planning, so I think it's fairly
      interesting story-wise-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0afee15b7c0b2ad4481946e7b9820870, type: 2}
    dialog: Are you sure you should be giving out spoilers while {Player} is watching?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 7856103185826971712
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: What?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: Oh.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 7856103185826971713
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: Uh...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: What are you even doing here-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: How did you even-?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: Why would you-!
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: You know what? Whatever.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fdd5cfec9471d2f48a6134838a2b377b, type: 2}
    dialog: Get the hell out of here!
    ScreenActions: []
